  "body": "## What's Changed\n* chore(nix): bump flake to 1.32.2 by @github-actions[bot] in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1983\n* Require that no commit, commit author or PR text credits an AI tool by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1991\n* Expose the VM's DMA-BUF heaps to containers so Android can allocate graphics buffers by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1992\n* Bump libkrunfw with the Android kernel options and the TSI socket fixes by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1993\n* Seed private registry images whose credentials arrive with the start by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1984\n* Give a checkpoint started during another one its share of workers by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1990\n* Bump zstd to 0.14.3 to clear four security advisories by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1997\n* Run the macOS CI job on our own Mac mini and keep its target/ between runs by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1999\n* Fix Docker socket forwarding into workload namespaces by @horjulf in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1998\n* Remove an ephemeral `machine run`'s data directory when the run fails before its VM starts by @RitikaxG in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1996\n* Let a frozen branch source stop once every branch of it is stopped by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/2003\n* Run the Linux x86_64 CI job on our own MS-A2, keeping target/ between runs by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/2005\n* Make the usage journal and engine-binary tests independent of tests running beside them by @BinSquare in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/2007\n\n## New Contributors\n* @horjulf made their first contribution in https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/pull/1998\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/smol-machines/smolvm/compare/v1.32.2...v1.32.4",
